d1_binding_and_platform_types.s:
Create the D1 database, declare its binding, and type `platform.env.PUZ` so every later step compiles.

WHY THIS FIRST: nothing else can be typed or run without the binding. `search_puzzles` currently reaches straight for `$env/static/private` (QDRANT_URL/QDRANT_KEY) and needs no request context; D1 is a *binding*, only reachable via `platform.env`, so the whole call chain changes shape. This step just makes the handle exist and typecheck.

FACTS ESTABLISHED (do not re-derive):
- D1 max database size is 10 GB on Workers Paid, 500 MB on Free. Max account storage 5 GB Free / 1 TB Paid. Rows written 100,000/day Free, 50,000,000/month Paid. THIS WORK REQUIRES WORKERS PAID — 6,014,381 puz rows + 29,702,004 pt rows will not fit or import on Free. If the account is Free, stop and tell the user.
- Repo already threads `platform` through handlers (grep: `src/routes/webhook/+server.ts:6`, `src/routes/+layout.server.ts:6`, `src/routes/chess/learn/chat/+server.ts:62`, `src/routes/api/puzzles/+server.ts` does NOT yet). Existing consumers (`credit`/`deduct`/`get_balance` in `src/lib/server/token_balance.ts`) take `_event: unknown` and ignore it — do NOT copy that pattern, we need the real binding.
- `worker-configuration.d.ts` does NOT exist and MUST NOT be generated. Global AGENTS.md forbids `wrangler types` in the build script and warns it breaks Cloudflare Workers Builds. We hand-declare the 4 D1 members we actually use instead — zero new deps, zero generated files.

