sql_dump_builder.s:
Write `scripts/build_puzzle_sql.mjs`: stream the 1 GB lichess CSV and emit chunked SQL files that `wrangler d1 execute --file` can ingest.

WHY A DUMP AND NOT A CLIENT LOOP: D1 has no bulk upsert API from Node. The supported bulk path is `wrangler d1 execute <db> --remote --file=x.sql` (verified against wrangler 4.101.0 — there is no `wrangler d1 import` subcommand). Max file import is 5 GB and max SQL STATEMENT length is 100,000 bytes, so rows must be batched into multi-row INSERTs under that cap and split across several files.

CSV FORMAT (verified): header `PuzzleId,FEN,Moves,Rating,RatingDeviation,Popularity,NbPlays,Themes,GameUrl,OpeningTags`. Fields never contain commas, so a plain `line.split(',')` is correct — do not add a CSV parser. Themes and OpeningTags are space-separated. OpeningTags is often empty.

FIELD MAPPING: index 0 PuzzleId, 1 FEN, 2 Moves, 3 Rating, 5 Popularity, 7 Themes, 9 OpeningTags. Indexes 4 (RatingDeviation), 6 (NbPlays) and 8 (GameUrl) are DROPPED — `GameUrl` alone is ~40 bytes x 6M = 240 MB of storage nobody reads, and the puzzle URL is derivable as `https://lichess.org/training/<PuzzleId>`.

